  "heading": "\\relation:?on{X}",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{relation on }X",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\relation:?on{X}]\nDeclares: R \\:subset:/ (.X \\.set.cross./ X.)\nwhen: X is \\set\nEnables:\n. capability: R(x_, y_) :=> (x_, y_) \"in\"? R\n  written: \"x_? \\: R \\: y_?\"\nDocumented:\n. called: \"relation on $X?$\"\n. description: \"A relation on a set $X$ is a subset $R$ of $X \\times X$. One\n                writes $x \\mathrel{R} y$ to mean that the pair $(x, y)$ belongs\n                to $R$, so a relation is just a precise record of which ordered\n                pairs are related.\"\nId: \"5ace60a2-cc66-4cea-818a-538f877b5f97\"",
